<title>FRANCE: Cie Bancaire 96 loss 1.2 bln Ffr. [CORRECTED 9:27 GMT]</title>
<headline>Cie Bancaire 96 loss 1.2 bln Ffr. [CORRECTED 9:27 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable		  loss 1,230  vs	profit 602</p>
<p>(Corrects 1996 figure from profit to loss)</p>
<p>    Net new provisions		     2,480		     N/A</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		   10    vs		same</p>
<p> Contributions from units to overall Cie Bancaire net result</p>
<p>    UFB local bail and units		 234  vs		 196</p>
<p>    Cetelem and units			1,320  vs	     1,155</p>
<p>    UCB and units		     loss 2,694  vs	  loss 438</p>
<p>     of which provisions	  charge 2,030  vs</p>
<p>    Klecar and units			   168  vs		  76</p>
<p> of which Klepierre</p>
<p>			    and units	    163  vs		 129</p>
<p> Sinvim</p>
<p>	   and units		    loss   659  vs	  loss 568</p>
<p>	of which provisions	 charge   230  vs 	Cardif and units			 332  vs		 298</p>
<p>Note - Cie Bancaire said its unit Cetelem posted a 1996 net attributable profit of 1.31 billion francs, up 16 percent from the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
